## 2. Workflow Bloat Prevention **[core]**

Keep repository workflows lightweight. Only introduce automations that serve active development goals.

### Do NOT Enable (for Solo/Personal Repositories):
- **Stale Issue/PR Managers (`stale.yml`)**: Unnecessary overhead that creates visual noise and automated notifications on inactive archives.
- **AI Issue Summarizers / GPT Autorepliers**: Increases API token costs and runs unnecessarily on private or single-developer repos.
- **Auto-Labeling Workflows**: Standard git branches and single-developer workflows do not need automated categorization overhead.

### Recommended Workflows (if needed):
- **Continuous Integration (CI)**: Running tests and building the production package on PR or push to `main` (e.g. `npm run test` and `npm run build`).
- **Deployments (CD)**: Deploying to staging or production (e.g., Cloudflare Pages, Vercel, Firebase App Hosting) on merge.
